      "title": "Signal-PDU: Fix performance degradation on config switch",
      "message": "Signal-PDU: Fix performance degradation on config switch\n\nBy adding signal aggregation the time to change profiles changed\ndramatically. This is due to unregistering header fields being a very\nslow operation and for aggregation each signal line did not lead to 2\nbut to 5 hfs.\n\nUnregistering header fields for 150k signal example config (debug build):\n- 3.6: \t 50s\n- 3.7: \t592s (9:52!!!)\n\nThis patch brings the time back to 50s, if no aggregation is configured.\n",
      "author_name": "Dr. Lars Völker",
      "author_email": "lars.voelker@technica-engineering.de",
      "authored_date": "2022-06-22T09:48:49.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "A Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2022-06-23T19:24:17.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
